# Copy to `.claude/private-patterns.local` — which is gitignored — and fill in.
#
# One extended-regex per line, matched case-insensitively against anything about
# to be written or committed. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# This file exists because the things it lists cannot live in a published file.
# The publishing rule bars the maintainer's own name from this repository, and
# the hook that matches on it is committed to this repository. So the shapes a
# matcher can derive on its own — RFC 1918 addresses, CGNAT space, MAC and OUI
# forms — are built into `.claude/hooks/no-estate-identity.sh`, and only the
# things it has to be TOLD go here.
#
# The hook refuses to run at all when the local copy is missing. That is
# deliberate: a fresh clone with no pattern list has no protection, and the one
# failure mode worse than no hook is a hook that looks like it is working.
#
# What belongs here:
#
#   - The maintainer's personal name, given and family, and any spelling of it
#     that would read as ordinary attribution. `foxythefoxer` is the identity
#     this repo publishes under and must NOT be listed — a GitHub handle is
#     public by construction.
#   - Email addresses.
#   - Hostnames of real machines in the estate, including short names. Identify
#     a host by class instead: "a Proxmox LXC", "the Unraid box".
#   - The name of the private notes vault, and the filenames of notes in it.
#     A citation like "per <some-note>.md, 2026-09-05 entry" reads as courtesy
#     inside the vault and as disclosure outside it.
#   - Any tailnet or LAN domain suffix.
#
# What does NOT belong here: hardware models, panel models, byte counts, file
# modes and timings. Those are the measurements that make an adjudication
# auditable, and they are publishable — a monitor anyone can buy is not estate
# identity.
#
# Anchor with \b where a fragment could appear inside an ordinary word.

# \bexample-hostname\b
# \bgiven-name\b
# \bfamily-name\b
# someone@example\.com
# \.example-tailnet\.ts\.net\b
# \bmy-notes-vault\b
